course: dictionary
lesson: 8235
title: Words that turn
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show movement, and revolve is one of them. To revolve means to move in a circle around a central point, or to turn around on its own centre like a wheel. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: Look at the sentence: «a restless revolving squirrel» (in a turning cage). A squirrel that cannot keep still, in a cage that is turning, must be moving round and round. Ask: what word would fit here? Turning fits, so revolving means turning.
explain: Revolve also has a bigger meaning. The Earth revolves around the Sun once a year, and it spins on its own axis once a day. When «his life revolves around football», football is the most important thing to him. Swap in a meaning to check: it still makes sense.
fact: Revolve is a verb: revolve, revolves, revolved, revolving.
fact: «Revolve» means to move in a circle around a central point.
fact: «Revolve» also means to turn around on its own centre, like a wheel.
fact: «Revolve around» something means having it as the most important thing.
fact: The Earth revolves around the Sun once a year and rotates on its axis once a day.
exercise: «a restless revolving squirrel» (in a turning cage). What does revolving mean here? | Eating nuts | Hiding under a cloth | *Turning round and round | Sleeping quietly
exercise: Which word means the Earth moves in a circle around the Sun? | Shrinks | *Revolves | Glows | Sleeps
exercise: «His life revolves around football.» What does this suggest? | He is going to the circus | He hates football | He plays football in a circle | *Football is the most important thing to him
test: Which meaning fits revolve when a wheel spins on its own centre? | *Turns around on its own centre | Falls over | Stands still | Shouts loudly
test: «a revolving door» goes round and round. What does revolving mean here? | Stuck and still | Heavy and made of glass | Open and shut | *Moving in a turning circle
exam: Jayden says revolve is just another word for spin, so it is mid. Why might an author choose revolve instead? | *It can mean moving around a centre, and also what matters most to someone | It is a colour | It is shorter
